    <briefdescription>
<para>Strict-weak comparator on integer indices into a <computeroutput>std::vector&lt;int*&gt;</computeroutput> of monomials, used by the resolution code to sort columns. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Each <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_sorter_object_ab6053ba650361723c9acf3676051d348_1ab6053ba650361723c9acf3676051d348" kindref="member">mMonoms</ref>[i]</computeroutput> is laid out as <computeroutput>[tiebreaker, basecomp, actual_monomial...]</computeroutput>. <computeroutput>operator()(a, b)</computeroutput> compares the monomial bodies via <computeroutput><ref refid="class_mono_monoid_a48d8666e2c503586cef03ee9bcc18589_1a48d8666e2c503586cef03ee9bcc18589" kindref="member">Monoid::compare</ref></computeroutput>, returning the corresponding <computeroutput><ref refid="classbool" kindref="compound">bool</ref></computeroutput>; on <computeroutput><ref refid="submodules_2mathicgb_2src_2mathicgb_2polyring_8hpp_abaab8d42f075ee8ddc9b70951d3fd6cd_1abaab8d42f075ee8ddc9b70951d3fd6cd" kindref="member">EQ</ref></computeroutput> it falls back to the <computeroutput>tiebreaker</computeroutput> slot. The static <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_sorter_object_a9b0cc6d192c59b2949169eca4a2971e5_1a9b0cc6d192c59b2949169eca4a2971e5" kindref="member">mNumComparisons</ref></computeroutput> counter records how many comparisons the sort performed <mdash/> handy when profiling a large frame&apos;s column-sort cost. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
